msgid "Machine page"
msgstr "Machine page"

msgid "![The Machine page](images/options-machine.png)"
msgstr "![La página Machine](images/options-machine.png)"

msgid "The Machine page"
msgstr "La página Machine"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This page sets up the running machine: **Model**, **Memory**, **ROM** and"
" the **Speed** slider at the top, then its devices in four groups - "
"**Storage**, **Input**, **Sound** and **Board**. The {icon}`settings` "
"gear beside a device opens the rest of its settings."
msgstr ""
"Esta página configura la máquina en marcha: **Model**, **Memory**, "
"**ROM** y el deslizador **Speed** arriba, y después sus dispositivos en "
"cuatro grupos: **Storage**, **Input**, **Sound** y **Board**. El "
"engranaje {icon}`settings` junto a un dispositivo abre el resto de sus "
"ajustes."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"What you change here is kept for this machine only. {icon}`save_all` "
"**Save machine...**, {icon}`refresh` **Restore machine** and "
"{icon}`cancel` **Delete this machine** are explained in [Your own "
"machines](#your-own-machines)."
msgstr ""
"Lo que cambias aquí se guarda solo para esta máquina. {icon}`save_all` "
"**Save machine...**, {icon}`refresh` **Restore machine** y {icon}`cancel`"
" **Delete this machine** se explican en [Your own machines](#your-own-"
"machines)."

msgid ""
"**File > Options...** opens **Options**; **Machine** is its first page. "
"At the top:"
msgstr ""
"**File > Options...** abre **Options**; **Machine** es su primera página."
" Arriba:"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Model** - the machine. The {icon}`settings` gear beside it opens "
"**Machine: Advanced Settings**."
msgstr ""
"**Model** — la máquina. El engranaje {icon}`settings` de al lado abre "
"**Machine: Advanced Settings**."

msgid "**Memory** - how much RAM the machine has."
msgstr "**Memory** — cuánta RAM tiene la máquina."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**ROM** - the ROM files in use; the {icon}`settings` button opens "
"**Machine: ROM**."
msgstr ""
"**ROM** — los archivos de ROM en uso; el botón {icon}`settings` abre "
"**Machine: ROM**."

msgid "**Speed** - the slider described in [Speed](#speed)."
msgstr "**Speed** — el control deslizante descrito en [Speed](#speed)."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{icon}`refresh` **Restore machine**, {icon}`save_all` **Save "
"machine...**, {icon}`cancel` **Delete this machine** - see [Your own "
"machines](#your-own-machines)."
msgstr ""
"{icon}`refresh` **Restore machine**, {icon}`save_all` **Save "
"machine...**, {icon}`cancel` **Delete this machine** — consulta [Your own"
" machines](#your-own-machines)."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Below them are the machine's devices, in four groups. Each row has a "
"choice and a {icon}`settings` gear button; the gear opens the rest of "
"that device's settings, in a window named after it, such as **Machine: "
"Disk**. A gray gear means the device has nothing more to set. **OK** "
"closes such a window and keeps what you set in it for **Apply**; "
"**Cancel** (or Esc) puts back what it showed when it opened."
msgstr ""
"Debajo están los dispositivos de la máquina, en cuatro grupos. Cada fila "
"tiene una opción y un botón de engranaje {icon}`settings`; el engranaje "
"abre el resto de los ajustes de ese dispositivo, en una ventana con su "
"nombre, como **Machine: Disk**. Un engranaje gris significa que el "
"dispositivo no tiene nada más que ajustar. **OK** cierra esa ventana y "
"guarda lo que ajustaste en ella para **Apply**; **Cancel** (o Esc) "
"devuelve lo que mostraba al abrirse."

msgid "Group"
msgstr "Grupo"

msgid "Row"
msgstr "Fila"

msgid "What it sets"
msgstr "Qué ajusta"

msgid "**Storage**"
msgstr "**Storage**"

msgid "**Tape**"
msgstr "**Tape**"

msgid "loading settings; the row shows which are on (see [Tapes](tapes.md))"
msgstr ""
"ajustes de carga; la fila muestra cuáles están activados (consulta "
"[Tapes](tapes.md))"

msgid "**Disk**"
msgstr "**Disk**"

msgid ""
"**None**, **Beta Disk (WD1793)** or **+3 (uPD765)**; drives and the TR-"
"DOS ROM in its window (see [Floppy disks](disks.md))"
msgstr ""
"**None**, **Beta Disk (WD1793)** o **+3 (uPD765)**; las unidades y la ROM"
" de TR-DOS en su ventana (consulta [Floppy disks](disks.md))"

msgid "**Hard disk**"
msgstr "**Hard disk**"

msgid ""
"the IDE interface; **Master** and **Slave** in its window (see [Hard "
"disks](sd-hdd.md#hard-disks))"
msgstr ""
"la interfaz IDE; **Master** y **Slave** en su ventana (consulta [Hard "
"disks](sd-hdd.md#hard-disks))"

msgid "**SD card**"
msgstr "**SD card**"

msgid ""
"ZX Evolution and ZX Spectrum Next only: the card in use (for the Next, "
"see [The SD card](zx-next.md#the-sd-card))"
msgstr ""
"solo ZX Evolution y ZX Spectrum Next: la tarjeta en uso (para el Next, "
"consulta [The SD card](zx-next.md#the-sd-card))"

msgid "**divMMC**"
msgstr "**divMMC**"

msgid ""
"48K, 128K, +2, +2A, +3 and the Pentagons: **None** or **divMMC**; RAM, "
"EEPROM jumper and the firmware in its window (see [divMMC](divmmc.md))"
msgstr ""
"48K, 128K, +2, +2A, +3 y los Pentagon: **None** o **divMMC**; la RAM, el "
"jumper de la EEPROM y el firmware en su ventana (consulta "
"[divMMC](divmmc.md))"

msgid "**Cartridge**"
msgstr "**Cartridge**"

msgid "48K and ALF only: the cartridge in use"
msgstr "solo 48K y ALF: el cartucho en uso"

msgid "**Input**"
msgstr "**Input**"

msgid "**Joystick**"
msgstr "**Joystick**"

msgid "**None**, **Kempston 5-bit**, **Kempston 8-bit**"
msgstr "**None**, **Kempston 5-bit**, **Kempston 8-bit**"

msgid "**Mouse**"
msgstr "**Mouse**"

msgid ""
"**None** or **Kempston mouse**; sensitivity and wheel in its window (see "
"[Mouse](input.md#mouse))"
msgstr ""
"**None** o **Kempston mouse**; sensibilidad y rueda en su ventana "
"(consulta [Mouse](input.md#mouse))"

msgid "**PC keyboard**"
msgstr "**PC keyboard**"

msgid ""
"ATM Turbo 2+ and ZX Evolution only: which scan codes the machine gets "
"(see [Machines with a keyboard of their own](input.md#machines-with-a"
"-keyboard-of-their-own))"
msgstr ""
"solo ATM Turbo 2+ y ZX Evolution: qué códigos de escaneo recibe la "
"máquina (consulta [Machines with a keyboard of their own](input.md"
"#machines-with-a-keyboard-of-their-own))"

msgid "**Sound**"
msgstr "**Sound**"

msgid "**PSG**"
msgstr "**PSG**"

msgid ""
"the AY/YM chips, from **None** to **x3 - ZX Next**; chip, clock and "
"stereo in its window (see [PSG](#psg))"
msgstr ""
"los chips AY/YM, de **None** a **x3 - ZX Next**; chip, reloj y estéreo en"
" su ventana (consulta [PSG](#psg))"

msgid "**DAC**"
msgstr "**DAC**"

msgid "**None**, **Covox only**, **Soundrive 1.05 mode 1** or **mode 2**"
msgstr "**None**, **Covox only**, **Soundrive 1.05 mode 1** o **mode 2**"

msgid "**General Sound**"
msgstr "**General Sound**"

msgid "**Off** or **On**; its ROM in its window"
msgstr "**Off** u **On**; su ROM en su ventana"

msgid "**SAA1099**"
msgstr "**SAA1099**"

msgid "**Off** or **On**"
msgstr "**Off** u **On**"

msgid "**Board**"
msgstr "**Board**"

msgid "**Turbo**"
msgstr "**Turbo**"

msgid "the turbo steps: **x1 (no turbo)**, **x1, x2** or **x1, x2, x4**"
msgstr "los pasos de turbo: **x1 (no turbo)**, **x1, x2** o **x1, x2, x4**"

msgid "**ESP UART**"
msgstr "**ESP UART**"

msgid ""
"ZX Spectrum Next only: **Not connected**, **ESP-01 (emulated)** - the Wi-"
"Fi module with Espressif's AT firmware 1.7.6, on this computer's network "
"- or a serial port of this computer with a real module on it. In its "
"window, **Server on the network** lets other computers reach a server the"
" module opens; off, only this computer can, at 127.0.0.1"
msgstr ""
"solo ZX Spectrum Next: **Not connected**, **ESP-01 (emulated)** — el "
"módulo Wi-Fi con el firmware AT 1.7.6 de Espressif, en la red de este "
"equipo — o un puerto serie de este equipo con un módulo real conectado. "
"En su ventana, **Server on the network** permite que otros equipos "
"lleguen a un servidor que abra el módulo; desactivado, solo puede este "
"equipo, en 127.0.0.1"

msgid "**Pi UART**"
msgstr "**Pi UART**"

msgid "ZX Spectrum Next only: a serial port of this computer for the Pi's UART"
msgstr ""
"solo ZX Spectrum Next: un puerto serie de este equipo para el UART de la "
"Pi"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Changes take effect when you press **Apply** or {icon}`ok-apply` **OK**."
msgstr "Los cambios surten efecto al pulsar **Apply** u {icon}`ok-apply` **OK**."

msgid "Speed"
msgstr "Speed"

msgid ""
"**Speed** on the **Machine** page of **Options** is a slider for the "
"whole emulation:"
msgstr ""
"**Speed** en la página **Machine** de **Options** es un control "
"deslizante para toda la emulación:"

msgid ""
"left of the middle, **Slow Motion 1/2**, **1/4** and **1/8** slow "
"everything down, and the frame rate drops with it;"
msgstr ""
"a la izquierda del centro, **Slow Motion 1/2**, **1/4** y **1/8** lo "
"ralentizan todo, y la frecuencia de fotogramas baja con ello;"

msgid "the middle is **Normal speed**;"
msgstr "el centro es **Normal speed**;"

msgid ""
"right of the middle, **Overclock x2**, **x4** and **x8** speed the CPU up"
" and keep the frame rate."
msgstr ""
"a la derecha del centro, **Overclock x2**, **x4** y **x8** aceleran la "
"CPU y mantienen la frecuencia de fotogramas."

msgid ""
"No real machine ran faster than 14 MHz, so past that the timing of a "
"program is not guaranteed. The slider is not saved: the next start is at "
"normal speed. The **Speed Up** and **Speed Down** hotkeys move it too. "
"See also [Speed and time](time.md)."
msgstr ""
"Ninguna máquina real funcionaba a más de 14 MHz, así que por encima de "
"eso la temporización de un programa no está garantizada. El control "
"deslizante no se guarda: el siguiente arranque es a velocidad normal. Los"
" atajos de teclado **Speed Up** y **Speed Down** también lo mueven. "
"Consulta también [Speed and time](time.md)."

msgid "Advanced settings"
msgstr "Advanced settings"

msgid ""
"**Machine: Advanced Settings** holds the settings of the hardware itself,"
" not of how you use it. Leave them alone unless you know the hardware."
msgstr ""
"**Machine: Advanced Settings** contiene los ajustes del propio hardware, "
"no de cómo lo usas. No los toques a menos que conozcas el hardware."

msgid ""
"**CPU** - **Base clock**, the frequency of the crystal the board runs on."
" The frame rate is derived from it too."
msgstr ""
"**CPU** — **Base clock**, la frecuencia del cristal con el que funciona "
"la placa. De ella sale también la frecuencia de fotogramas."

msgid ""
"**ULA** - **Raster layout** (the size of the frame and where the "
"interrupt falls in it), **ULA pattern**, **Floating bus**, **Ear input**,"
" and check boxes for **Contended memory**, **Contended I/O**, **Early "
"timings**, **4T border**, **ULA snow...**, **...and it crashes**, **MIC "
"in the beeper** and **ULA plus**."
msgstr ""
"**ULA** — **Raster layout** (el tamaño del fotograma y dónde cae en él la"
" interrupción), **ULA pattern**, **Floating bus**, **Ear input** y "
"casillas para **Contended memory**, **Contended I/O**, **Early timings**,"
" **4T border**, **ULA snow...**, **...and it crashes**, **MIC in the "
"beeper** y **ULA plus**."

msgid "**Board** - **Even M1** (Scorpion ZS 256) and **DD palette** (Profi)."
msgstr "**Board** — **Even M1** (Scorpion ZS 256) y **DD palette** (Profi)."

msgid ""
"Each one is explained beside it, or in a tooltip when you hold the mouse "
"over it."
msgstr ""
"Cada uno se explica a su lado, o en una descripción emergente al dejar el"
" ratón encima."

msgid "Machine: Tape"
msgstr "Machine: Tape"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"On the **Machine** page of **Options**, the **Storage** group has a "
"**Tape** row. It sums up the settings: **plain**, or the ones that are "
"on: **fast**, **flash**, **edge**, **auto**. By default all four are on. "
"The {icon}`settings` button at the end of the row opens the **Machine: "
"Tape** sheet:"
msgstr ""
"En la página **Machine** de **Options**, el grupo **Storage** tiene una "
"fila **Tape**. Resume los ajustes: **plain**, o los que están activados: "
"**fast**, **flash**, **edge**, **auto**. Por defecto, los cuatro están "
"activados. El botón {icon}`settings` al final de la fila abre el panel "
"**Machine: Tape**:"

msgid "**Playback speed**;"
msgstr "**Playback speed**;"

msgid "**Auto play / stop**;"
msgstr "**Auto play / stop**;"

msgid "**Rewind at end**;"
msgstr "**Rewind at end**;"

msgid "**Fast loading**, **Flash loading** and **Edge detection**."
msgstr "**Fast loading**, **Flash loading** y **Edge detection**."

msgid ""
"The first four are the same settings as in the **Tape Player**, where a "
"change takes effect at once."
msgstr ""
"Los cuatro primeros son los mismos ajustes que en el **Tape Player**, "
"donde un cambio surte efecto al instante."

msgid ""
"The tape's loudness is **Tape** in the **Volumes** group of the **Sound**"
" page (see [Sound page](options-sound.md))."
msgstr ""
"El volumen de la cinta es **Tape** en el grupo **Volumes** de la página "
"**Sound** (consulta [Sound page](options-sound.md))."

msgid "Machine: Disk"
msgstr "Machine: Disk"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The {icon}`settings` gear in the **Disk** row of the **Machine** page "
"opens **Machine: Disk**:"
msgstr ""
"El engranaje {icon}`settings` de la fila **Disk** de la página "
"**Machine** abre **Machine: Disk**:"

msgid ""
"**Fast disk access** - no waiting for the head to move or the disk to "
"turn; see [Fast Disk Access](disks.md#fast-disk-access)."
msgstr ""
"**Fast disk access** — sin esperar a que el cabezal se mueva o el disco "
"gire; consulta [Fast Disk Access](disks.md#fast-disk-access)."

msgid "**Add boot loader** - see [The boot file](disks.md#the-boot-file)."
msgstr "**Add boot loader** — consulta [The boot file](disks.md#the-boot-file)."

msgid "**TR-DOS ROM** - which ROM image the Beta Disk runs."
msgstr "**TR-DOS ROM** — qué imagen de ROM ejecuta el Beta Disk."

msgid ""
"**Interleave** - the order of sectors on each track of a `.trd` or `.scl`"
" image, set when the image is opened. TR-DOS formats its own disks as 1, "
"9, 2, 10..."
msgstr ""
"**Interleave** — el orden de los sectores en cada pista de una imagen "
"`.trd` o `.scl`, fijado al abrir la imagen. TR-DOS formatea sus propios "
"discos como 1, 9, 2, 10..."

msgid ""
"**Number of drives** - from one (A) to four (A to D); a +3 has two at "
"most. A drive left out is not there at all, and programs find it missing."
msgstr ""
"**Number of drives** — de una (A) a cuatro (de la A a la D); un +3 tiene "
"dos como mucho. Una unidad que se quita no existe en absoluto, y los "
"programas la encuentran ausente."

msgid "**Drives** - for each drive, **80 cylinders** and **Double side**."
msgstr "**Drives** — para cada unidad, **80 cylinders** y **Double side**."

msgid "Sound devices"
msgstr "Sound devices"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The **Sound** group on the **Machine** page of **Options** lists the "
"sound devices of the running machine. Each machine keeps its own devices:"
" a change here applies to this machine only. The button with the "
"{icon}`settings` gear at the end of a row opens the device's further "
"settings. How loud each device plays is set on the [Sound page](options-"
"sound.md)."
msgstr ""
"El grupo **Sound** de la página **Machine** de **Options** lista los "
"dispositivos de sonido de la máquina en marcha. Cada máquina guarda sus "
"propios dispositivos: un cambio aquí afecta solo a esta máquina. El botón"
" con el engranaje {icon}`settings` al final de una fila abre el resto de "
"los ajustes del dispositivo. Lo fuerte que suena cada dispositivo se fija"
" en la [Sound page](options-sound.md)."

msgid "PSG"
msgstr "PSG"

msgid ""
"The PSG is the sound chip most music on the Spectrum is written for. The "
"**PSG** row sets how many of them the machine has:"
msgstr ""
"El PSG es el chip de sonido para el que está escrita la mayor parte de la"
" música del Spectrum. La fila **PSG** fija cuántos tiene la máquina:"

msgid "Choice"
msgstr "Opción"

msgid "What you get"
msgstr "Qué obtienes"

msgid "**None**"
msgstr "**None**"

msgid "no sound chip"
msgstr "ningún chip de sonido"

msgid "**x1 - AY/YM**"
msgstr "**x1 - AY/YM**"

msgid "one chip, three voices - the 128K machines and most clones"
msgstr "un chip, tres voces — las máquinas de 128K y la mayoría de los clones"

msgid "**x2 - TurboSound**"
msgstr "**x2 - TurboSound**"

msgid "two chips, six voices, for music written for TurboSound"
msgstr "dos chips, seis voces, para música escrita para TurboSound"

msgid "**x2 - TurboSound FM**"
msgstr "**x2 - TurboSound FM**"

msgid ""
"two YM2203 chips: TurboSound with FM synthesis, for music written for "
"TurboSound FM"
msgstr ""
"dos chips YM2203: TurboSound con síntesis FM, para música escrita para "
"TurboSound FM"

msgid "**x3 - ZX Next**"
msgstr "**x3 - ZX Next**"

msgid "three chips, nine voices"
msgstr "tres chips, nueve voces"

msgid ""
"A program written for one chip plays on the first chip of two or three, "
"and sounds the same."
msgstr ""
"Un programa escrito para un chip suena en el primero de dos o tres chips,"
" y suena igual."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The {icon}`settings` gear opens **Machine: PSG**:"
msgstr "El engranaje {icon}`settings` abre **Machine: PSG**:"

msgid ""
"**Chip** - **AY-3-8910** or **YM2149**. The two sound alike; the YM2149 "
"plays volume envelopes in finer steps. **YM2203** is the chip of "
"TurboSound FM: choosing **x2 - TurboSound FM** sets it, and the list is "
"then grayed out."
msgstr ""
"**Chip** — **AY-3-8910** o **YM2149**. Los dos suenan parecido; el YM2149"
" reproduce las envolventes de volumen en pasos más finos. **YM2203** es "
"el chip de TurboSound FM: al elegir **x2 - TurboSound FM** se fija este "
"chip, y la lista aparece entonces en gris."

msgid ""
"**Clock** - the chip's clock in MHz, which sets the pitch. **Auto** is "
"half the machine's base CPU clock, as the boards divide it, and the list "
"shows the resulting value. **1.773447** is the clock of the ZX Spectrum "
"128, +2 and +3; **1.75** that of most clones. Music written for one of "
"them sounds a little out of tune on the other. You can also type a clock "
"of your own."
msgstr ""
"**Clock** — el reloj del chip en MHz, que fija el tono. **Auto** es la "
"mitad del reloj base de la CPU de la máquina, como lo dividen las placas,"
" y la lista muestra el valor resultante. **1.773447** es el reloj del ZX "
"Spectrum 128, +2 y +3; **1.75**, el de la mayoría de los clones. La "
"música escrita para uno de ellos suena algo desafinada en el otro. "
"También puedes escribir un reloj propio."

msgid ""
"**Stereo** - **Mono**, or the order of the three voices from left to "
"right: **ABC**, **ACB**, **BAC**, **BCA**, **CAB**, **CBA**. **ABC** puts"
" the second voice in the middle; **ACB** puts the third voice there."
msgstr ""
"**Stereo** — **Mono**, o el orden de las tres voces de izquierda a "
"derecha: **ABC**, **ACB**, **BAC**, **BCA**, **CAB**, **CBA**. **ABC** "
"pone la segunda voz en el centro; **ACB** pone ahí la tercera."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Separation** - how far apart the left and right sides are: 100% keeps "
"them fully apart, 0% is mono. It is grayed out with **Mono**."
msgstr ""
"**Separation** — cuánto se separan los lados izquierdo y derecho: 100% "
"los separa por completo, 0% es mono. Aparece en gris con **Mono**."

msgid "DAC"
msgstr "DAC"

msgid ""
"A DAC plays digitized sound - speech, drums and samples - written to a "
"port byte by byte:"
msgstr ""
"Un DAC reproduce sonido digitalizado — voz, percusión y samples — escrito"
" en un puerto byte a byte:"

msgid "**None** - no DAC;"
msgstr "**None** — sin DAC;"

msgid "**Covox only** - one mono channel on port #FB;"
msgstr "**Covox only** — un canal mono en el puerto #FB;"

msgid ""
"**Soundrive 1.05 mode 1** - four channels, two on each side, on ports "
"#0F, #1F (left) and #4F, #5F (right);"
msgstr ""
"**Soundrive 1.05 mode 1** — cuatro canales, dos por lado, en los puertos "
"#0F, #1F (izquierda) y #4F, #5F (derecha);"

msgid ""
"**Soundrive 1.05 mode 2** - the same four channels on ports #F1, #F3 "
"(left) and #F9, #FB (right)."
msgstr ""
"**Soundrive 1.05 mode 2** — los mismos cuatro canales en los puertos #F1,"
" #F3 (izquierda) y #F9, #FB (derecha)."

msgid "Pick the one the program is written for."
msgstr "Elige aquel para el que está escrito el programa."

msgid "General Sound"
msgstr "General Sound"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A sound card with a processor and memory of its own, which plays music "
"modules and samples for the programs written for it. **On** puts it in "
"the machine. The {icon}`settings` gear opens **Machine: General Sound**:"
msgstr ""
"Una tarjeta de sonido con procesador y memoria propios, que reproduce "
"módulos de música y samples para los programas escritos para ella. **On**"
" la pone en la máquina. El engranaje {icon}`settings` abre **Machine: "
"General Sound**:"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**ROM** - the card's own ROM, picked from the list or from a file with "
"the {icon}`fileopen` folder button;"
msgstr ""
"**ROM** — la ROM propia de la tarjeta, elegida de la lista o de un "
"archivo con el botón de carpeta {icon}`fileopen`;"

msgid "**Reset** - the card is reset together with the machine."
msgstr "**Reset** — la tarjeta se reinicia junto con la máquina."

msgid "SAA1099"
msgstr "SAA1099"

msgid ""
"A sound chip with six voices, found on some sound cards for the Spectrum."
" **On** puts it in the machine."
msgstr ""
"Un chip de sonido de seis voces, presente en algunas tarjetas de sonido "
"para el Spectrum. **On** lo pone en la máquina."

msgid "Your own machines"
msgstr "Your own machines"

msgid ""
"A change you make to a machine stays with that machine. It is saved when "
"you apply it and when you switch to another machine, so when you come "
"back to that machine, you find it as you left it. Each machine keeps its "
"own: memory, the ROM set and the marked ROM, base clock, turbo steps, the"
" **Advanced settings**, and its devices - disk interface and number of "
"drives, hard disk interface, PSG, DAC, General Sound, SAA1099, joystick, "
"mouse and PC keyboard. The other settings on the page, such as the tape "
"settings, are the same for every machine."
msgstr ""
"Un cambio que haces en una máquina se queda con esa máquina. Se guarda al"
" aplicarlo y al cambiar a otra máquina, así que al volver a esa máquina "
"la encuentras como la dejaste. Cada máquina conserva lo suyo: la memoria,"
" el juego de ROM y la ROM marcada, el reloj base, los pasos de turbo, los"
" **Advanced settings** y sus dispositivos — interfaz de disco y número de"
" unidades, interfaz de disco duro, PSG, DAC, General Sound, SAA1099, "
"joystick, ratón y teclado de PC. Los demás ajustes de la página, por "
"ejemplo los ajustes de la cinta, son iguales para todas las máquinas."

msgid ""
"A built-in machine you have changed gets an asterisk after its name. It "
"still gets the fixes that a new version of Xpeccy+ brings, in every "
"setting you did not change."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina incorporada que has cambiado lleva un asterisco tras su "
"nombre. Sigue recibiendo las correcciones que trae una nueva versión de "
"Xpeccy+, en cada ajuste que no cambiaste."

msgid "The three buttons on the **Machine** page:"
msgstr "Los tres botones de la página **Machine**:"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{icon}`save_all` **Save machine...** saves the current settings as a new "
"machine under a name you give (Xpeccy+ suggests the machine's name with "
"`(mine)` after it). The new machine appears in the machine list and runs "
"at once. It is based on the machine it was made from, so it too gets that"
" machine's fixes in every setting you did not change. The name must be "
"one no other machine has."
msgstr ""
"{icon}`save_all` **Save machine...** guarda los ajustes actuales como una"
" máquina nueva con el nombre que le des (Xpeccy+ propone el nombre de la "
"máquina con `(mine)` detrás). La máquina nueva aparece en la lista de "
"máquinas y se pone en marcha al instante. Se basa en la máquina de la que"
" se hizo, así que también recibe las correcciones de esa máquina en cada "
"ajuste que no cambiaste. El nombre no puede coincidir con el de otra "
"máquina."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{icon}`refresh` **Restore machine** undoes every change. A built-in "
"machine goes back to its original settings; one of your own goes back to "
"the settings of the machine it was made from, and stays in the list."
msgstr ""
"{icon}`refresh` **Restore machine** descarta todos los cambios. Una "
"máquina incorporada vuelve a sus ajustes originales; una tuya vuelve a "
"los ajustes de la máquina de la que se hizo, y sigue en la lista."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{icon}`cancel` **Delete this machine** removes a machine of your own, "
"after asking, and switches to the one it was made from. Built-in machines"
" cannot be deleted: use **Restore machine**."
msgstr ""
"{icon}`cancel` **Delete this machine** elimina una máquina tuya, tras "
"preguntar, y cambia a aquella de la que se hizo. Las máquinas "
"incorporadas no se pueden eliminar: usa **Restore machine**."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each machine you have changed or made is a small text file in the "
"`machines` folder of the settings folder (see [Where the settings are"
"](getting-started.md#where-the-settings-are)). It holds only what differs"
" from the machine it is based on. Deleting the file of a built-in "
"machine, with Xpeccy+ closed, does the same as **Restore machine**. "
"{icon}`save_all` **Export settings...** on the **Application** page "
"exports your own machines together with the settings."
msgstr ""
"Cada máquina que has cambiado o creado es un pequeño archivo de texto en "
"la carpeta `machines` de la carpeta de ajustes (consulta [Where the "
"settings are](getting-started.md#where-the-settings-are)). Solo contiene "
"lo que difiere de la máquina en la que se basa. Borrar el archivo de una "
"máquina incorporada, con Xpeccy+ cerrado, hace lo mismo que **Restore "
"machine**. {icon}`save_all` **Export settings...** en la página "
"**Application** exporta tus propias máquinas junto con los ajustes."

msgid "ROM images"
msgstr "ROM images"

msgid ""
"The ROM images are in the `roms` folder of the settings folder. Xpeccy+ "
"comes with every image its machines need. The images come under their own"
" license terms: `LICENSE` and `PROVENANCE.md` in the same folder say "
"where each one came from."
msgstr ""
"Las imágenes de ROM están en la carpeta `roms` de la carpeta de ajustes. "
"Xpeccy+ trae todas las imágenes que necesitan sus máquinas. Las imágenes "
"tienen sus propias condiciones de licencia: `LICENSE` y `PROVENANCE.md` "
"en la misma carpeta dicen de dónde viene cada una."

msgid ""
"To replace a ROM for every machine that uses it, put your file into "
"`roms` under the same name. On Linux and macOS a new version of Xpeccy+ "
"adds the images it is missing but never overwrites one that is already "
"there, so your file stays."
msgstr ""
"Para sustituir una ROM en todas las máquinas que la usan, pon tu archivo "
"en `roms` con el mismo nombre. En Linux y macOS, una nueva versión de "
"Xpeccy+ añade las imágenes que faltan pero nunca sobrescribe una que ya "
"está, así que tu archivo se queda."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To give one machine a different ROM, click the {icon}`settings` **ROM** "
"button on the **Machine** page. The **Machine: ROM** window lists the "
"machine's ROM banks, named after what is in each, such as **ROM 0 (Basic "
"128)**:"
msgstr ""
"Para dar a una máquina otra ROM, haz clic en el botón {icon}`settings` "
"**ROM** de la página **Machine**. La ventana **Machine: ROM** muestra los"
" bancos de ROM de la máquina, con el nombre de lo que hay en cada uno, "
"como **ROM 0 (Basic 128)**:"

msgid ""
"pick a file from the list, which holds every `.rom` and `.bin` file in "
"the `roms` folder;"
msgstr ""
"elige un archivo de la lista, que contiene todos los archivos `.rom` y "
"`.bin` de la carpeta `roms`;"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"or click the {icon}`fileopen` folder button beside it to pick a file from"
" any folder;"
msgstr ""
"o haz clic en el botón de carpeta {icon}`fileopen` de al lado para elegir"
" un archivo de cualquier carpeta;"

msgid "mark the bank a plain reset starts from (**Boots from the marked ROM**)."
msgstr ""
"marca el banco desde el que arranca un reinicio normal (**Boots from the "
"marked ROM**)."

msgid ""
"**Font** is the text-mode font, for the machines that have one. The "
"General Sound ROM is in the **Machine: General Sound** window, and the "
"TR-DOS ROM in **Machine: Disk**."
msgstr ""
"**Font** es la fuente del modo texto, para las máquinas que lo tienen. La"
" ROM de General Sound está en la ventana **Machine: General Sound**, y la"
" ROM de TR-DOS en **Machine: Disk**."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{icon}`settings` **Expert settings** opens **Machine: ROM Files**, the "
"same ROM set shown file by file: where each part starts in its file, how "
"much of it is read, and where it is placed in the machine's ROM. Its "
"buttons {icon}`add` add a file, {icon}`edit` edit or {icon}`cancel` "
"remove the one selected, and {icon}`lamp` fill the set with the machine's"
" standard ROMs again. Adding or editing opens the **Romset Editor** with "
"**File**, **File offset**, **Size** (0 reads to the end of the file) and "
"**ROM pos**, all in KB."
msgstr ""
"{icon}`settings` **Expert settings** abre **Machine: ROM Files**, el "
"mismo juego de ROM mostrado archivo por archivo: dónde empieza cada parte"
" en su archivo, cuánto se lee de ella y dónde se coloca en la ROM de la "
"máquina. Sus botones {icon}`add` añaden un archivo, {icon}`edit` editan o"
" {icon}`cancel` quitan el seleccionado, y {icon}`lamp` vuelven a llenar "
"el juego con las ROM estándar de la máquina. Añadir o editar abre el "
"**Romset Editor** con **File**, **File offset**, **Size** (0 lee hasta el"
" final del archivo) y **ROM pos**, todo en KB."

msgid ""
"The new ROM is in place when you press **Apply**. Reset the machine to "
"start from it."
msgstr ""
"La nueva ROM queda puesta al pulsar **Apply**. Reinicia la máquina para "
"arrancar desde ella."

